    "landing_reviews_iExUAA": {
      "type": "landing-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "review_tFVf6t": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "avatar": "shopify://shop_images/Screenshot_2026-09-22_at_07.55.25_1.jpg",
            "show_stars": true,
            "text": "<p>Honestly, I’ve got 100 things going on, and when my little one asks “<em>Dad, what are we doing today?</em>”, my creativity isn’t exactly at its peak. 😅<br/><br/>Here you just open the book, pick what you’re doing, and it’s all written out step by step. And in the end you come out looking like the Jordan of dads 😂<br/><br/>The best part is the kids are completely hooked. I don’t have to think about what we’re doing anymore – now the two of them keep nagging about which mission is next.<br/><br/>I don’t know if the book made me a better dad. But I definitely look like I always have an ace up my sleeve :)</p>",
            "name": "Jure Prinčič, Slovenia (translated)"
          }
        },
        "review_zfDjGb": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "avatar": "shopify://shop_images/CC9B492B-DBFD-483E-8613-31F6290A14BD.webp",
            "show_stars": true,
            "text": "<p>As a grandma, I happily bought the book for my son-in-law, because it gives what I think is the most precious thing – <strong>time together.</strong><br/><br/>It’s full of fun ideas that get a dad and his kid to experience something together, laugh and, above all, enjoy each other – because that’s exactly where the memories kids keep forever come from.</p>",
            "name": "Simone S."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "review_tFVf6t",
        "review_zfDjGb"
      ],
