    "landing_letter_xqjbdb": {
      "type": "landing-letter",
      "name": "Landing: Letter",
      "settings": {
        "avatar": "shopify://shop_images/image_7.webp",
        "heading": "“I’m no parenting expert. But I’m pretty well trained in nonsense.”",
        "body": "<p><strong>I’m not a parenting expert. Not even close.</strong> I’m a dad of two girls and I deal with the same problems as every other dad: confusion, helplessness, pretending I know what I’m doing, and the feeling that I’ll miss everything that matters.</p><p>But I do know one thing. For most of my life <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">I’ve been turning ordinary situations into stories, shows and nonsense that people enjoy.</span></p><p>That’s why I created the I Am Best Dad In The World kit. Not to lecture dads on how to raise their kids, but so that when we hear <strong>“</strong><em><strong>What are we doing today?</strong></em><strong>” we don’t have to invent the answer all over again.</strong></p><p><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">I tested the missions at home. On my own kids.</span> Some ended in laughter, some in a mess, the best ones in both. They turned into moments we still talk about.</p><p>If this kit <strong>helps you show up for your kid more often, pull something off and really be there, it’s done its job.</strong> If it also makes you the family hero for a few minutes, I won’t complain.</p><p><strong>— From the author himself, Lado</strong></p>",
        "background_color": "#ffffff",
